    "sanity_floor": 0.9,
    "scaled_run_reason": "f32 confirms exclusion, not selection. R-4 extrapolates f32 at ~17GB against AC-46's 16GB ceiling, so it is over the ceiling before measurement and cannot become the answer at any scale. Disk on this shared box could not hold 15.6GiB of f32 shards plus the 12GiB reserve, and the reserve was deliberately NOT lowered to make it fit. 2M vectors measures bytes-per-vector exactly: on-disk growth is dead linear across shards, verified in the corrected run at i8 (0.50/0.99/1.49/1.98/2.48 GiB over shards 0-4, 532 B/vector at 10M) and f16 (0.85/1.71/2.56/3.41/4.27/5.12 GiB, 114s/shard). Shard-0 recall is measured per 1M shard in EVERY precision, so this run's recall and ef-sweep are directly comparable to i8's and f16's rather than approximations. What this does NOT give is 10M-corpus query latency for f32, which is neither measured nor claimed - f32 is excluded on RAM, so its latency never enters the decision.",
